<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John George, Elector of Brandenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1525–1598</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John George was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> from 1571 to 1598, a Hohenzollern prince and strict Lutheran. In 1571 he inherited both the electorate and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neumark">Neumark</a> of his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-margrave-of-brandenburg-kustrin">John of Küstrin</a>, reuniting the Brandenburg lands. A thrifty ruler, he paid down his father's debts, expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> from Brandenburg and avoided foreign wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-george-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="John George, Elector of Brandenburg" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brandenburg_Court_miniaturist_(Royal_Collection)_-_Johann_Georg,_Elector_of_Brandenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
